Implementation should not start from this specification. I'm not editing any artefacts. My review is saved in `reviews/2026-10-17/distill-review-1.md`.

```yaml
verdict: "NEEDS_REWORK"
confidence: "medium"
lenses:
  coverage: {status: fail, findings: [G1 BLOCKER Gold 8400 vs AC-3 8500, G1 BLOCKER AC-4 has no scenario, G2 HIGH no boundary or rounding case]}
  business-alignment: {status: pass, findings: []}
  testability: {status: fail, findings: [G9 BLOCKER outer test repeats 8_400, G10 BLOCKER test fails at compile and is not RED on an assertion, G6 HIGH impl plan has no per-scenario entries, G5 HIGH rounding direction ambiguous, G11 LOW test file naming]}
  boundary-enforcement: {status: fail, findings: [G7 HIGH contracts file missing, G8 HIGH no walking skeleton]}
synthesis:
  questions:
    completeness: {answered_by: [coverage], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.00}
    business-fit: {answered_by: [business-alignment], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.30}
    quality: {answered_by: [testability], weight: 0.15, contribution: 0.00}
    risk: {answered_by: [boundary-enforcement], weight: 0.25, contribution: 0.125}
  blocking_findings: [Gold 8400 vs 8500, AC-4 unscenarioed, outer test encodes 8400, outer test not RED]
  dissent: "Business-alignment passes. Not overridden, because the other lenses' failures are value and coverage defects that independently block."
```

**What would let wrong behaviour through**
- **Gold price:** The feature and the outer test both expect 8400, but AC-3 says 8500. Following the test, Gold would get a 16% discount.
- **Rounding:** The AC-4 rounding case (Bronze, 7 cents) has no scenario, so rounding is untested. The author's "full coverage" claim is false, because the coverage matrix drops AC-4.
- **AC-4 contradiction:** AC-4 says "in the customer's favour", but charging 7 cents for a 7-cent basket rounds against the customer (5% of 7 is 6.65). The product owner needs to settle this before anything is built.
- **Not RED:** No production types exist (`CalculateLoyaltyDiscount`, `LoyaltyTier` and so on), so the outer test fails at compile. It never fails on a business assertion.
- **Plans:** The implementation plan has no per-scenario entries. There is no contracts file and no walking skeleton.
